{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467224-the-big-short","id":1467224,"title":"\"The Big Short\"","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-08T19:41:20-08:00","id":1467224,"title":"\"The Big Short\"","content":"Which magical groups would the characters in the movie &quot;The Big Short&quot; be in if they were Mage characters?<br /> <br /> Mark Baum?<br /> <br /> Michael Burry?<br /> <br /> Jared Vennett?<br /> <br /> Ben Rickert?<br /> <br /> Charlie Geller and Jamie Shipley?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T23:47:56-08:00","id":1467236,"title":"","content":"Baum is a Syndicate agent that's using the housing bubble burst to analyze the rest as potential recruits either as extraordinary citizens or possibly financial types on the verge of Enlightenment from seeing how the system breaks without a strong Syndicate hand on things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-10T22:50:10-08:00","id":1467416,"title":"","content":"I've always enjoyed the idea of the 2008 financial crisis being the product of an extended Syndicate hyper-economics procedure suffering a devastating Paradox backlash/&quot;Market Correction&quot;; thus the big banks, and credit bureaus, were probably just the Syndicate trying to pull a financial rabbit out of their hat. The brokers and what not at the subprime mortgage <i>sales</i> level who understood that they were getting people into houses they couldn't afford, and into mortgages that could balloon and ruin them, those are your Nephandi; the realtors and brokers under <i>them</i>, who weren't necessarily aware of the scam-in-fact or the particulars, but still had the niggling sense that <i>&quot;this is too good to be true/there's a catch here somewhere</i><i>&quot;</i> but still made their money off the rank and file... those are your Nephandi prospects.<br /> <br /> Finally, and with regard to the players on the &quot;good guys&quot; side (i.e., saw it coming, tried to throw up a flare, invested in a manner that has been born out as wise based on their ultimately accurate prediction of the imminent collapse of the house of cards,) -- I feel l they're portrayed (in the <i>Big Short</i> as well as in other pieces and written accounts,) as relatively insular, &quot;alpha&quot; finance and fintech types who probably don't play well with others. I would lean towards considering those moreso Orphans than &quot;dues-paying&quot; or card carrying members of any given tradition; and if they <i>are </i>members of a more regimented tradition, they would probably have some kind of dispensation to operate hyper autonomously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T05:59:02-08:00","id":1467436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467224-the-big-short?p=1467416#post1467416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would lean towards considering those moreso Orphans than &quot;dues-paying&quot; or card carrying members of any given tradition; and if they <i>are </i>members of a more regimented tradition, they would probably have some kind of dispensation to operate hyper autonomously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think they're simply Sleepers most of the time.<br /> <br /> To be accurate, <b><i>they're the witnesses</i></b>, Sleepers with enough knowledge to see the bubble as Vulgar Magic and that decided to look into it instead of giving a blind eye.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T11:27:10-08:00","id":1467459,"title":"","content":"Baum comes across as the Syndicate at their best: a true believer who genuinely thinks that everyone would benefit from a strong, corruption-free economy. He's the kind of guy who would still be the antagonist in a Tradition-centric game, but an honorable antagonist who views both the Traditions and those among his own group who treat the masses as sheep as worthy of contempt.<br /> <br /> As far as he is concerned, both groups are just hurting people. The Traditions are hurting people by trying to con them into believing in hocus-pocus that will ultimately destroy them economically. The corrupt among the Technocracy by using their superior ability in a short-sighted, honorless, greedy way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3598,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","user":"CajunKhan","date":". 11-11-2021, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T14:13:44-08:00","id":1467476,"title":"","content":"Also, I hate the idea of &quot;market corrections&quot; as some sort of Paradox issue. I'm fine with the Technocracy believing that to cover up for their own failings, but not on a metaphysical level.<br /> <br /> These things happen because people make concrete decisions. The movie is called &quot;The Big Short&quot; because people chose to short for immediate economic benefit (which they got a lot of) without regard to the long term consequences. It wasn't some random change event, or a natural disaster, or even some sort of Rube Goldberg-esque series of highly improbable events. It was a bunch of people acting on a variety of influences making choices; which some people realized was pushing things in a horrible direction.<br /> <br /> If a mage tosses a fireball, misses, and hits a building that burns down, we know that any attempt to blame Paradox is bull. That's just the consequences of a character making their choices.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T15:49:59-08:00","id":1467491,"title":"","content":"If you were using Primal Utility to draw Quintessence from investments that suddenly become Toxic Assets, I could see some kind of Paradox afflicting the Mage, given the public nature of the crisis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T15:53:29-08:00","id":1467492,"title":"","content":"Prime can do that too, now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T15:54:41-08:00","id":1467493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467224-the-big-short?p=1467492#post1467492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime can do that too, now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Is that from Rich Bastards?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T16:01:16-08:00","id":1467496,"title":"","content":"Yes, it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-11T19:39:06-08:00","id":1467512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1467224-the-big-short?p=1467476#post1467476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I hate the idea of &quot;market corrections&quot; as some sort of Paradox issue. I'm fine with the Technocracy believing that to cover up for their own failings, but not on a metaphysical level.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can buy the idea of it involving a bit of Paradox because I know how most economists think.<br /> <br /> A big chunk of economic theory do believe that with a sufficiently advanced system we can create value inside the market in a sustainable way. As much as the crisis is obvious in hindsight and some people thought so at the time, a lot of serious and professional investors and economists sincerely believed they had things tightly in control. The crisis actually got worse because of that.<br /> <br /> While reality didn't actually worked like that, and we can say for certain that the crisis isn't some Paradox effect because the Crisis was a thing, Paradox isn't, it does makes sense in the setting:<br /> <br /> The Syndicate tried to create wealth out of nothing. It is easy to just picture them as greedy investors, but they <b>are</b> Mages, they <b>are</b> trying to make their super-economics theories work, and they don't really like a crisis. They <b>do</b> apply Magic to the market that <b>can </b>create wealth out of nothing.<br /> <br /> So, what does a Paradox Effect looks like in such a situation? It isn't actually restrained by the market, despite their theories. It may worsen the effects of the burst and create stranger outcomes in its midst. Being Paradox as it is, it may ignore causation and start taking root before the actual ritual. It may not be the whole of the crisis, that being more the magic being unraveled, but be a part of the sting it had despite decades of experience controlling crisis.<br /> <br /> Most importantly in this scenario, though, it is Paradox, and Paradox isn't an aimless force. The thing with the crisis being a Paradox Effect isn't that it will somewhat explain the suffering of millions. It will explain the suffering of a very particular group of few who had the resources to stand the crisis, and yet failed miserably.<br /> <br /> Not to say that in the scenario of a bubble being the result of a Syndicate magical effect, it is probable that its burst wasn't actually accepted. It makes sense to happen, but if it was meant to make sense it wouldn't be Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}